is there a powertoy to append folder size to each name in within a folder of folders
No official Microsoft PowerToy can append folder sizes directly to directory names. Windows File Explorer does not calculate or display folder sizes in real time because doing so across large directory trees can cause severe system lag.
However, you can accomplish this cleanly using a PowerShell script or a third-party tool.

Method 1: PowerShell Script (Built-in, No Extra Software)
This script iterates through every subfolder in a target directory, calculates its total size in megabytes or gigabytes, and renames the folder to include that size (e.g., Documents becomes Documents [1.2 GB]).

PowerShell
$TargetDirectory = "C:\Path\To\Your\Folder"

Get-ChildItem -Path $TargetDirectory -Directory | ForEach-Object {
    $Folder = $_
    
    # Calculate total size of all files inside the subfolder
    $SizeBytes = (Get-ChildItem -Path $Folder.FullName -Recurse -File -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | 
                  Measure-Object -Property Length -Sum).Sum
                  
    if ($null -ne $SizeBytes) {
        # Format size into MB or GB
        if ($SizeBytes -ge 1GB) {
            $FormattedSize = "{0:N2} GB" -f ($SizeBytes / 1GB)
        } else {
            $FormattedSize = "{0:N2} MB" -f ($SizeBytes / 1MB)
        }
        
        # Define new folder name
        $NewName = "$($Folder.Name) [$FormattedSize]"
        
        # Rename the folder
        Rename-Item -Path $Folder.FullName -NewName $NewName -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    }
}
Note: If you run this script multiple times on the same folder, it will keep appending new sizes to the existing names.

Method 2: Third-Party Utility Alternatives
If you prefer a visual, dedicated tool rather than running scripts, these utilities handle folder size calculations or advanced renaming:
TreeSize Free / WizTree: These tools do not rename the folders on disk, but they scan directory trees instantly and display folder sizes right next to their names in a clean UI.
Bulk Rename Utility: A specialized Windows batch renamer that allows flexible regex and criteria rules if you need to strip or re-format appended size strings later.
